3. BASIC TECHNICAL TERMINOLOGY
============================================================

CitiML:
A structured representation of financial transaction
information using XML elements.

XML:
A format for representing structured information.

XSD:
XML Schema Definition. Defines the structure, elements,
data types and rules of an XML document.

XPath:
A path that identifies the location of an element inside
an XML hierarchy.

Node:
An individual element within the XML/XPath structure.

Dictionary:
A container representing a data model in Data Catalog.

Example:
CITIML
CitiMLTest

Concept:
A collection inside a Data Catalog dictionary.

Concept in the API corresponds to Collection in the
MetaManager UI.

Attribute:
A field inside a concept or collection.

Self Attribute:
An attribute created with the same name as its concept,
used as an anchor for creating relationships.

Relationship:
A metadata connection between two registered objects.

Symlink:
A symbolic metadata link between Data Catalog objects.

Attribute Symlink:
A relationship connecting one or more attributes to
other attributes.

Lineage:
Information describing how data originates, flows,
or is derived from another data element.

In our current POC, the LINEAGE relationship type is
being used to represent XML parent-child connections.

This is a hierarchy representation workaround.
It does not mean that actual transaction data is
being transferred between these XML nodes.

Portable Identifier:
A unique identifier assigned by Data Catalog to a
metadata object, relationship or reference record.

Cardinality:
Describes how objects can participate in a relationship.

Our POC uses:
ANY

Transformation Logic:
Describes the relationship or transformation between
source and target attributes.

Our POC uses:
DIRECT

No actual data transformation is performed by our POC.


