5. DATA CATALOG COMPONENTS
============================================================

DATA CATALOG:

The central metadata platform where dictionaries,
collections, attributes and relationships are registered.

DATА HIGHWAY:

The API service layer used to interact with Data Catalog.

METAMANAGER:

The administrative UI for managing and viewing
Data Catalog metadata and relationships.

MetaManager can be used to:

- View dictionaries.
- Browse collections.
- Browse attributes.
- View existing relationships.
- Manage relationships.
- Check relation status.

DATA CATALOG BROWSER:

The user-facing UI for discovering and navigating
published metadata and lineage information.

SWAGGER:

API documentation and testing interface.

It describes:

- Available API endpoints.
- HTTP methods.
- Request parameters.
- Request JSON structure.
- Response JSON structure.
- Authentication requirements.

Swagger is not the Data Catalog database.
It is documentation and an interface for calling APIs.

SOAPUI:

A tool for making and testing API requests manually.

Although the application is named SoapUI, it can also
call REST APIs with JSON.

Our POC uses REST APIs, not SOAP/XML web services.

NOTEPAD++:

Used to inspect, prepare and format JSON payloads and
API responses.


