26. RELATIONSHIP BETWEEN OUR WORK AND RUPESH'S LINEAGE
============================================================

There are two different kinds of relationships
to understand.

A. INTERNAL CITIML HIERARCHY

This is our current POC.

Example:

TradeNotification
    -> NotificationBundleDetails
    -> Events

It describes parent-child relationships between
elements within the same CitiML structure.


B. ACTUAL DATA LINEAGE

This describes where data comes from and how it
flows or is transformed across source and target
systems or data models.

Illustrative example:

Source trade field
    -> CitiML trade attribute
    -> Downstream consumer field

Rupesh's work provides relevant XPath and lineage
information for the wider integration activity.

Our current POC establishes how to register the
CitiML metadata and represent its internal hierarchy.

Both activities may use attribute-to-attribute
relationship APIs.

However, the meaning of the relationships is
different.

Do not confuse the current XML parent-child links
with actual source-to-target data movement.

The exact ownership and scope of future end-to-end
lineage implementation should be confirmed with
Rajat and Rupesh.


